description: Core App Router + layer conventions (slim)
globs: src/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Core

- App Router only. Routes orchestrate; keep `page`/`layout` thin.
- Placement: route → `app/<route>/_components/<name>/`; home/layout → `app/_components/`; shared ≥2 routes → `components/` (`ui/` flat).
- Reuse before redesign: existing shared/UI/`_components` first — extend with props; do not rebuild chrome per page (see `components.mdc`).
- Folder-per-component: `<name>/index.tsx` — never `_components/foo.tsx`.
- `lib/` = env/http/helpers; `utils/` = API client helpers; `providers/` / `hooks/` / `types/` as needed.
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only for interactivity.
- Env: `src/lib/env.ts` (plain defaults, or Zod/Yup when scaffolded). HTTP via `lib/http` or `utils/api` / `endpoints` — not scattershot `fetch`.
- Direction: `useDirection()` from `@/hooks/use-direction` — do not set `dir` ad hoc on random nodes.
- i18n (when `.cursor/rules/i18n.mdc` exists): pages/layouts under `app/[locale]/`; prefer `@/i18n/navigation` + message keys over hardcoded copy/`next/link`.
- Named exports `function Name()`; default exports only for Next route files.
- One `<main>` in root layout only.
- If you change these conventions, update this rule + `AGENTS.md` + `docs/style-guide/` together.
